This covers the data files in `apps/web/public/`, and `boxes.json` in
particular: the catalogue of boxed sets, what each one holds, when it was
announced, and where that was read from.

WHAT IS CLAIMED, AND WHAT IS NOT

No claim is made over the underlying facts. That a given boxed set contains ten
of a unit is a fact about a product somebody else sells, and facts are nobody's
property. Every entry names the page its contents were read from, and those
pages belong to their own publishers.

The claim is over the compilation: which boxes are listed, how their contents
are recorded against a game's datasheets, the corrections applied to make the
two agree, and the arrangement of the whole. That is the work — each box was
read off a published source, and each unit was checked against a full game-data
snapshot and corrected where the marketing name and the datasheet name differ.

In the European Union and the United Kingdom this compilation is asserted as a
database in which there has been substantial investment in obtaining and
verifying the contents, and the maker's rights in it are reserved
(Directive 96/9/EC and the equivalent retained law).

TERMS

You may not extract or re-use the whole, or a substantial part, of this
compilation without prior written permission.

You may quote individual entries — to correct one, to discuss one, or to cite
one — with attribution to this project.

CONTRIBUTIONS

A correction or an addition submitted to this repository may be included here
under these terms. Contributions are welcome; the catalogue is far from
complete, and a box added with its source is worth more than a box guessed at.
